.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \(dqbashclient.h\(dq

int bc_send_msg(bc_client_t *c, int channel, const char *json);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends a raw JSON message on the specified v2 protocol channel.
The \f[B]json\f[R] string is the payload content without framing; the
library adds the appropriate wire framing (NDJSON or binary) based on
the negotiated wire format.
.PP
This is a \f[B]low\-level function\f[R] intended for protocol
extensions, debugging, or cases where the channel\-specific convenience
functions (e.g., \f[CR]bc_pty_spawn(3)\f[R], \f[CR]bc_eval(3)\f[R]) are
insufficient.
Most callers should prefer the higher\-level functions.
.SH Wire framing
\f[B]NDJSON mode\f[R] (default): The message is sent as a single line:
.IP
.EX
{\(dqch\(dq:<channel>,...json fields...}\(rsn
.EE
.PP
The library merges the \f[CR]\(dqch\(dq\f[R] field into the JSON object.
The \f[B]json\f[R] parameter should contain the inner fields without the
outer braces or \f[CR]\(dqch\(dq\f[R] field.
For example, if \f[B]json\f[R] is
\f[CR]\(dq\(rs\(dqaction\(rs\(dq:\(rs\(dqping\(rs\(dq\(dq\f[R] and
\f[B]channel\f[R] is 0, the wire output is:
.IP
.EX
{\(dqch\(dq:0,\(dqaction\(dq:\(dqping\(dq}\(rsn
.EE
.PP
\f[B]Binary mode\f[R]: The message is sent as a 6\-byte header followed
by the JSON payload.
The \f[B]json\f[R] parameter is used as\-is for the payload.
The \f[CR]\(dqch\(dq\f[R] field is not automatically inserted in binary
mode (the channel is in the header).
