.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
In NDJSON mode, the library constructs the final JSON object by
prepending \f[CR]{\(dqch\(dq:N,\f[R] and appending \f[CR]}\(rsn\f[R] to
the \f[B]json\f[R] parameter.
The \f[B]json\f[R] string must therefore be the inner key\-value pairs
without surrounding braces.
.IP \(bu 2
In binary mode, the \f[B]json\f[R] parameter is sent as\-is (it should
be a complete JSON object).
The channel and flags are in the binary header.
.IP \(bu 2
This function is synchronous: it blocks until the entire frame is
written to the transport fd.
It does not wait for a server response; use \f[CR]bc_recv_msg(3)\f[R] to
read the response.
.IP \(bu 2
Sending on a channel that requires prior setup (e.g.,
\f[CR]CHAN_PTY\f[R] without a spawn) may cause server\-side errors.
The server\(cqs error response arrives as a frame on the same channel.
.IP \(bu 2
The function is not thread\-safe.
Do not call \f[CR]bc_send_msg\f[R] and \f[CR]bc_recv_msg\f[R]
concurrently from different threads on the same client handle.
